# Only send the files needed to build the image to the build context
*
# The package: code, config and API specifications only, so that other local
# files in it (e.g., config copies, logs) don't reach the image; the wheel
# takes only the package data listed in `pyproject.toml` of these
!drs_filer/**/*.py
!drs_filer/config.yaml
!drs_filer/api/*.yaml
!LICENSE
!pyproject.toml
# The lock, from which the image build installs the dependencies
!uv.lock
!README.md
# Run by the image build to list the requirements to install
!scripts/image_requirements.py

# Exclude caches and local files within the included paths
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
# Modified API specifications (written at runtime by some FOCA versions)
drs_filer/api/*.modified.yaml
# Local secrets (e.g., `.env`, `.env.local`, `.envrc`) must never reach the
# build, also not within the included paths; no example is re-included, as
# the build copies none (and an exception with wildcards makes Docker walk
# all excluded directories)
**/.env*
# Other common names of secret files
**/*.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/.git-credentials
**/.pypirc
**/credentials*.json
**/.netrc
